---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="dollarlint documentation"
  description="A custom Astro documentation site for the dollarlint CLI."
  current="/"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">CLI documentation</span>
    <h1>dollarlint</h1>
    <p class="hero-copy">
      Validate JSON, YAML, and TOML files against their declared JSON Schemas.
      dollarlint keeps config checks explicit, readable, and CI-friendly.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="/guides/quick-start/">Start validating</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="/reference/cli/">Read the CLI reference</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" aria-label="Highlights">
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Schema-first discovery</h3>
      <p>Files can declare schemas in JSON, YAML, or TOML. Files without a schema are skipped and reported in the run summary.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>CI-ready output</h3>
      <p>Choose grouped text, structured JSON, or SARIF 2.1.0 for code scanning and automation workflows.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Controlled remote fetching</h3>
      <p>Use retries, timeouts, allowlists, blocklists, and catalog matching to make remote schema use predictable.</p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="doc">
    <h2>Common commands</h2>
    <div class="command-list">
      <div class="command">
        <code>dollarlint init</code>
        <p>Create a starter <code>.dollarlint.toml</code> in the current directory.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="command">
        <code>dollarlint validate .</code>
        <p>Validate discovered JSON, YAML, and TOML files below the current directory.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="command">
        <code>dollarlint validate ./config --locations</code>
        <p>Show line and column positions in text output.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
